Author: Danny Milosavljevic <dannym@friendly-machines.com>
Date: 2026-05-10
Subject: Use first char address for ngtcon byte buffers
License: expat

`compiler/ngtcon.pas` uses a local `array[0..1] of char` as scratch
storage for one-character constants, then reads that scratch storage through
a `pbyte` cursor.

The original `ca := @ch` relies on assigning the address of the whole array
to a byte pointer.  Point at the first character explicitly instead; this
keeps the same byte-buffer semantics while avoiding a whole-array pointer
conversion in the translated bootstrap.

--- a/compiler/ngtcon.pas
+++ b/compiler/ngtcon.pas
@@ -1161,7 +1161,7 @@ implementation
                     else
                       internalerror(2010033002);
                   end;
-                  ca:=@ch;
+                  ca:=pbyte(@ch[0]);
                   len:=1;
                 end
              else if is_constwidecharnode(n) and (current_settings.sourcecodepage<>CP_UTF8) then
@@ -1179,7 +1179,7 @@ implementation
                     else
                       internalerror(2010033002);
                   end;
-                  ca:=@ch;
+                  ca:=pbyte(@ch[0]);
                   len:=1;
                 end
